{"abstract":"This paper reports from an ongoing research project on meaningful adoption and use of Generative Artificial Intelligence within the Communication Department of a Danish Municipality. Given its capacity to generate images, information, and text, GenAI models are positioned as being potentially transformative to cognitive tasks in knowledge work, raising concerns about skill displacement and a loss of meaning in the profession. This paper presents a set of sociotechnical principles for the introduction and integration of novel technologies, such as GenAI, while retaining meaningfulness in work. These principles were crafted by combining work design theory and extensive empirical material gathered through Action Design Research, in close collaboration with employees from the department. Centering the need for a common understanding of expectations for GenAI, the principles also point to the importance of organizational support to enable autonomous experimentation and accountability, while emphasizing transparency surrounding the decision-making process for the use of GenAI.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Marttila, Sanna-Maria","Sandbukt, Sunniva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759406"],"event":{"acronym":"ECIS","title":"European Conference on Information Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Action Design Research","Generative AI","Sociotechnical Principles","Work design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crafting meaningful generative ai enabled knowledge work","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106309094/Crafting_Meaningful_Generative_AI-Enabled_Knowledge_Work.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759406","ids":["itu-6aac332a-122b-4b49-a315-91b5cb88a459"],"keyword":["Action Design Research","Generative AI","Sociotechnical Principles","Work design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-567D1CDC6155A62357BE8A87B85C5BF4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106309094/Crafting_Meaningful_Generative_AI-Enabled_Knowledge_Work.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanna-Maria","key":"marttilapau","last":"Marttila","locid":"528393a3-e784-47a8-85be-c81d44c393bd","name":"Marttila, Sanna-Maria","orcid":"0000-0003-3793-5021","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sunniva","key":"sandbuktpau","last":"Sandbukt","locid":"06d038a4-f659-4c53-8a6d-58e295ab603f","name":"Sandbukt, Sunniva","orcid":"0009-0002-4274-4991","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000034"],"issue":"2024","journal":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","paperid":"10","status":"p","title":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","title_org":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems (ECIS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6aac332a-122b-4b49-a315-91b5cb88a459"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Crafting Meaningful Generative AI-Enabled Knowledge Work","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759406","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In April 2023, the Danish Emergency Management Agency (BRS) launched Denmark’s new mobile-based public warning system, SIRENEN. The new system uses cell-broadcast technology, supplementing the existing 1078 emergency sirens in the country, and replacing the voluntary ‘Mobilvarsling’ app. The new system will be managed by a consortium of government authorities led by BRS. This case ethnographically follows these actors as well as other stakeholder groups through the launch of the new system, its first nationwide test in May 2023, and the following months of establishing daily operational routines. Rather than treating this new system as a routine technological modernization of a central social infrastructure, this case centers the practical and political work of the various people engaged in making the system both technically operational, as well as publicly acceptable. In other words, it explores how this process involves not just technical, but also political change, and ultimately changes in the relations between citizens and the state. Drawing on existing research on the digital state in a Scandinavian context, the paper illustrates how managing a digital public warning system is not just a technological challenge, but also a careful process of maintaining public trust.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Sandbukt, Sunniva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712522"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digitalisation","Emergency communication","Ethnography","Scandinavia","Social infrastructure","Trust"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"managing sirenen maintaining both a technological system and public trust","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-712522","ids":["itu-5e5ca1be-b3c7-4735-9279-40c8d08e11de"],"keyword":["Digitalisation","Emergency communication","Scandinavia","ethnography","social infrastructure","trust"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4085368E8F2AF1152E7706D51AE2DE4D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, ETHOS Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sunniva","key":"sandbuktpau","last":"Sandbukt","locid":"06d038a4-f659-4c53-8a6d-58e295ab603f","name":"Sandbukt, Sunniva","orcid":"0009-0002-4274-4991","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5e5ca1be-b3c7-4735-9279-40c8d08e11de"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Managing SIRENEN : Maintaining both a technological system and public trust","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712522","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
